## Investigation Report: On-Color Alert Variants in Pendo Renderer

### 1. Current `hr` Rule in chrome.css

[chrome.css](renderers/pendo/src/css/chrome.css#L55-L62) (lines 55–62):
```css
hr {
  border-width: var(--instui-component-shared-tokens-stroke-width-sm);
  border-style: var(--instui-component-view-border-style);
  margin: var(--instui-component-shared-tokens-spacing-general-space-xs) var(--pendo-space-0);
  border-radius: var(--instui-component-shared-tokens-border-radius-full);
  border-color: var(--instui-color-stroke-muted);
}
```

### 2. Exact On-Color Stroke Token Name

**`--instui-color-stroke-on-color`** — defined in [formats/tokens/generated/canvas.json](formats/tokens/generated/canvas.json) and other theme variants.
- **Canvas theme**: resolves to `var(--instui-primitive-color-white)` (white)
- **CanvasHighContrast theme**: resolves to white
- **Rebrand theme**: resolves to `light-dark(var(--instui-primitive-color-sea-sea100), var(--instui-primitive-color-grey-grey180))` (light-dark aware)

### 3. Alert On-Color Selector Pattern

The core selector pattern used in [container.css](renderers/pendo/src/css/container.css#L325-L420) for scoping alert layouts:

```css
:scope[class*="instui-alert"][data-layout="lightboxBlank"] {
  /* Color variant selectors nested here */
  &[class*="-info"] { ... }
  &[class*="-danger"] { ... }
  &[class*="-success"] { ... }
  &[class*="-warning"] { ... }
}
```

**Key points:**
- Uses `:scope` to anchor at the root container
- `[class*="instui-alert"]` — detects alert class (attribute contains)
- `[data-layout="lightboxBlank"]` — specifies alert layout (not banner or popover)
- Nested `&[class*="-{color}"]` — matches `-info`, `-danger`, `-success`, `-warning` modifiers

### 4. Alert On-Color Token Usage

In [container.css](renderers/pendo/src/css/container.css#L325-L360), each color variant sets private CSS properties:

```css
&,
&[class*="-info"] {
  --_alert-background: var(--instui-component-alert-info-background);
  --_alert-border-color: var(--instui-component-alert-info-border-color);
  --_alert-glyph: var(--instui-icon-info);
  --_alert-icon-color: var(--instui-color-icon-on-color);
  --_alert-text-color: var(--instui-component-text-base-on-color);
}

&[class*="-danger"] {
  --_alert-background: var(--instui-component-alert-danger-background);
  --_alert-border-color: var(--instui-component-alert-danger-border-color);
  --_alert-glyph: var(--instui-icon-circle-x);
  --_alert-icon-color: var(--instui-color-icon-on-color);
  --_alert-text-color: var(--instui-component-text-base-on-color);
}

&[class*="-success"] {
  --_alert-background: var(--instui-component-alert-success-background);
  --_alert-border-color: var(--instui-component-alert-success-border-color);
  --_alert-glyph: var(--instui-icon-circle-check);
  --_alert-icon-color: var(--instui-color-icon-on-color);
  --_alert-text-color: var(--instui-component-text-base-on-color);
}

&[class*="-warning"] {
  /* Warning is deliberately NOT on-color — uses base text/icon instead */
  --_alert-background: var(--instui-component-alert-warning-background);
  --_alert-border-color: var(--instui-component-alert-warning-border-color);
  --_alert-glyph: var(--instui-icon-triangle-alert);
  --_alert-icon-color: var(--instui-color-text-base);
  --_alert-text-color: var(--instui-color-text-base);
}
```

### 5. Form Input On-Color Treatment

In [inputs.css](renderers/pendo/src/css/inputs.css#L538-L550), elevated alerts (non-warning) receive on-color form styling:

```css
/* ─── On-color (elevated alert) ─── */
/* Elevated alerts use inverse/on-color actions except warning, which is excluded here 
   so it falls through to the standard colours set above — no restatement needed. */
:is(:scope, [class*="instui"])[class*="instui-alert"][data-layout="lightboxBlank"]:not(
    [class*="-warning"]
  ) {
  &:not([class*="-warning"]) {
    /* Form controls styled for on-color backgrounds (info, danger, success alerts) */
    /* Warning alerts excluded; they maintain standard foreground colors */
  }
}
```

### 6. Non-Alert Exclusion Pattern

In [card.css](renderers/pendo/src/css/card.css#L36-L43), the pattern to **exclude** alerts from banner styling shows the inverse selector:

```css
/* Row spacing in Banner layout */
:is([data-layout="lightboxBlank"], [class*="instui-banner"]):not([class*="instui-alert"])
  ._pendo-row {
  margin-bottom: var(--instui-component-shared-tokens-spacing-gap-cards-md);
}
```

### 7. Available On-Color Tokens (from formats/components)

Related on-color tokens available in the palette [formats/components](formats/components):
- `--instui-color-icon-on-color` (used for alert icons)
- `--instui-component-text-base-on-color` (used for alert text in info/danger/success)
- `--instui-color-text-base-on-color` (text utilities)
- `--instui-component-base-button-primary-on-color-*` (button states)
- `--instui-color-stroke-on-color` ← **The stroke variant for dividers/borders**

### 8. Summary for Your `hr` Rule Update

**Current state:** `border-color: var(--instui-color-stroke-muted);` applies uniformly to all dividers.

**Planned pattern:** To make `hr` inherit on-color treatment inside alert variants, you'd scope it like:

```css
/* Global hr (current) */
hr {
  border-color: var(--instui-color-stroke-muted);
}

/* On-color variant — inside elevated alerts (info/danger/success only) */
:scope[class*="instui-alert"][data-layout="lightboxBlank"]:not([class*="-warning"]) hr {
  border-color: var(--instui-color-stroke-on-color);
}
```

This follows the exact selector precedent already established for form inputs in [inputs.css](renderers/pendo/src/css/inputs.css) and maintains the warning-alert exclusion convention.
